; kramanusara chain: jerk = d(acceleration)/d(time) = d³(displacement)/d(time)³
; L·T⁻³: three applications of kramanusara wrt time
; apeksha: kramanusara wrt physics-time, held in a sthira (fixed) reference frame
; spanda: jerk is where the derivative chain meets vibration
; in SHM, jerk = -omega² * velocity — the felt oscillation

(kosha jerk
  (vishesa linear-motion-varga)
  (abheda vivartana spanda)
  (yukta krama)
  (kramanusara acceleration)
  (sthita sthira-apeksha))
